.TH snip-edit 1 "" "snip 0.6.2" "Snip Manual"
.SH "NAME"
snip\-edit \- modify and organize snippets
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
\fBsnip edit\fR [\fB\-\-create\fR] [\fB\-\-title\fR] [\fB\-\-folder\fR] [\fB\-\-tag\fR] [\fB\-\-clear\-tags\fR] [\fB\-\-pin\fR] [\fB\-\-unpin\fR] [\fB\-\-lock\fR] [\fB\-\-unlock\fR] [\fB\-\-fragment\fR] [\fB\-\-fragment\-title\fR] [\fB\-\-language\fR] [\fB\-\-content\fR] [\fB\-\-content\-file\fR] [\fB\-\-note\fR] [\fB\-\-note\-file\fR] [\fB\-\-clear\-note\fR] [\fB\-\-readme\fR] [\fB\-\-readme\-file\fR] [\fB\-\-clear\-readme\fR] [\fB\-\-metadata\-editor\fR] [\fB\-\-readme\-editor\fR] [\fB\-\-note\-editor\fR] [\fB\-\-if\-hash\fR] [\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fISELECTOR\fR> 
\fBsnip fragment\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
\fBsnip fragment add\fR <\fB\-\-title\fR> [\fB\-\-language\fR] [\fB\-\-content\fR] [\fB\-\-content\-file\fR] [\fB\-\-note\fR] [\fB\-\-note\-file\fR] [\fB\-\-if\-hash\fR] [\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fISELECTOR\fR> 
\fBsnip fragment edit\fR [\fB\-\-title\fR] [\fB\-\-language\fR] [\fB\-\-content\fR] [\fB\-\-content\-file\fR] [\fB\-\-note\fR] [\fB\-\-note\-file\fR] [\fB\-\-clear\-note\fR] [\fB\-\-if\-hash\fR] [\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fISELECTOR\fR> <\fIFRAGMENT\fR> 
\fBsnip fragment remove\fR [\fB\-\-if\-hash\fR] [\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fISELECTOR\fR> <\fIFRAGMENT\fR> 
\fBsnip fragment reorder\fR <\fB\-\-position\fR> [\fB\-\-if\-hash\fR] [\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fISELECTOR\fR> <\fIFRAGMENT\fR> 
\fBsnip folder\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
\fBsnip folder list\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
\fBsnip folder create\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIFOLDER\fR> 
\fBsnip folder rename\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIFOLDER\fR> <\fINEW_NAME\fR> 
\fBsnip folder move\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIFOLDER\fR> <\fITARGET\fR> 
\fBsnip folder delete\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIFOLDER\fR> 
\fBsnip tag\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
\fBsnip tag list\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
\fBsnip tag rename\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fITAG\fR> <\fINEW_NAME\fR> 
\fBsnip tag delete\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fITAG\fR> 
\fBsnip organize\fR [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Modify snippet metadata and content, manage fragments, organize physical folders and tags, and normalize package directory names. Mutations use staged filesystem transactions and advisory locking.
.PP
Every read reports a BLAKE3 fingerprint computed from the snippet manifest, README, fragments, and notes. For a safe read\-modify\-write, read the current fingerprint and pass it back with \-\-if\-hash. If another writer changed the snippet, snip exits with conflict instead of overwriting it. Carry new_fingerprint from a successful mutation into the next write.
.PP
Use \-\-force only when overwriting concurrent changes or bypassing a lock is intentional. Folder rename changes one path component; folder move accepts a full destination path. Fragment positions are 1\-based.
.PP
The external\-editor form accepts \-\-create to create a missing snippet before opening it. It cannot be combined with \-\-if\-hash or content and metadata mutation flags; use snip create for non\-interactive creation. On a missing selector, \-\-folder, \-\-tag, and \-\-language configure the new snippet. A selector containing a slash uses everything before the final slash as the folder and the final component as the title.
.PP
Global options are described in snip(1).
.SH "COMMANDS"
.SS "snip edit"
Modify a snippet or launch an external editor
.TP
\fB\-\-create\fR
Create the snippet when the selector matches nothing, then open the editor
.TP
\fB\-\-title\fR \fI<TITLE>\fR
Replace the snippet title
.TP
\fB\-\-folder\fR \fI<FOLDER>\fR
Move the snippet to this folder. Pass "" for Uncategorized
.TP
\fB\-\-tag\fR \fI<TAGS>\fR
Replace tags with this tag set. Repeatable
.TP
\fB\-\-clear\-tags\fR
Remove every tag from the snippet
.TP
\fB\-\-pin\fR
Pin the snippet
.TP
\fB\-\-unpin\fR
Unpin the snippet
.TP
\fB\-\-lock\fR
Lock the snippet against mutation
.TP
\fB\-\-unlock\fR
Unlock the snippet
.TP
\fB\-\-fragment\fR \fI<FRAGMENT>\fR
Target fragment for structured changes or external editing
.TP
\fB\-\-fragment\-title\fR \fI<FRAGMENT_TITLE>\fR
Replace the selected fragment title
.TP
\fB\-\-language\fR \fI<LANGUAGE>\fR
Replace the selected fragment syntax language
.TP
\fB\-\-content\fR \fI<CONTENT>\fR
Replacement fragment content, given inline
.TP
\fB\-\-content\-file\fR \fI<CONTENT_FILE>\fR
Read replacement fragment content from a UTF\-8 file; use \- for stdin
.TP
\fB\-\-note\fR \fI<NOTE>\fR
Replacement fragment note (Markdown), given inline
.TP
\fB\-\-note\-file\fR \fI<NOTE_FILE>\fR
Read the replacement fragment note from a UTF\-8 file; use \- for stdin
.TP
\fB\-\-clear\-note\fR
Remove the selected fragment note
.TP
\fB\-\-readme\fR \fI<README>\fR
Replacement snippet README (Markdown), given inline
.TP
\fB\-\-readme\-file\fR \fI<README_FILE>\fR
Read the replacement snippet README from a UTF\-8 file; use \- for stdin
.TP
\fB\-\-clear\-readme\fR
Remove the snippet README
.TP
\fB\-\-metadata\-editor\fR
Edit snippet.toml in the external editor when no structured change is given
.TP
\fB\-\-readme\-editor\fR
Edit README.md in the external editor when no structured change is given
.TP
\fB\-\-note\-editor\fR
Edit the selected fragment note instead of its content
.TP
\fB\-\-if\-hash\fR \fI<IF_HASH>\fR
Refuse the write unless the snippet still has this fingerprint
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Bypass fingerprint checks and locked\-snippet protection
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fISELECTOR\fR>
Snippet title, UUID prefix, or package path
